       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Amlodipine 50 mg is five times the maximum recommended adult dose of 10 mg once daily. The usual range is 2.5\u201310 mg. A dose that high risks severe hypotension, reflex tachycardia, peripheral edema, and prolonged toxicity, because amlodipine has a long half-life. Kidney and liver function are normal, so nothing in the patient's profile explains it.\n\nThis may be a typo, for example 5 mg or 10 mg. Which of these do you want?\n\n- **5 mg** by mouth once daily, the standard starting dose.\n- **10 mg** by mouth once daily, the maximum dose.\n- **2.5 mg** by mouth once daily, a lower starting dose sometimes used in frail or older patients.\n- **50 mg**, if it's truly intended. I'd need you to confirm that and give the clinical rationale, and I'd add that to the order note.\n\nOnce you confirm the dose, I'll enter the order right away."
